The application should expose a single prompt entity with only these fields: `id`, `title`, `content`, `orderKey`, `createdAt`, and `updatedAt`. Prompt IDs must be UUIDs, `title` must be a non-empty trimmed string with a maximum length of 256 characters, and `content` must be a non-empty string with a maximum length of 100,000 characters. The prompt schema must be strict: removed legacy/advanced fields such as `scope`, `assistantId`, `variables`, `currentVersion`, version history, rollback data, or other unknown fields must be rejected.

The shared data API should include Prompt CRUD and ordering endpoints under `/prompts`. `GET /prompts` should return all prompts ordered by `orderKey`. `POST /prompts` should accept only `title` and `content` and return the created prompt. `GET /prompts/:id` should return a prompt by UUID. `PATCH /prompts/:id` should accept a partial update containing `title`, `content`, or both, but must reject an empty body with the message `At least one field is required`. `DELETE /prompts/:id` should delete the prompt. Ordering should be supported through the existing order endpoint pattern for `/prompts/:id/order` and `/prompts/order:batch`. Removed prompt-versioning APIs such as `/prompts/:id/versions` and `/prompts/:id/rollback` should not be exposed.

Prompt API handlers should validate all request parameters and bodies at the IPC/API boundary using the shared schemas. Invalid UUID path parameters, empty titles or content, over-limit values, empty update payloads, and removed fields must fail validation before reaching the service layer. Valid requests should delegate to the prompt service methods for list, get, create, update, delete, single reorder, and batch reorder.

The data layer should include a `prompt` SQLite table with columns for `id`, `title`, `content`, `order_key`, `created_at`, and `updated_at`, plus an index on `order_key`, so prompts persist in the same v2 data system as other entities. Migration cleanup/reset logic should include the new prompt table. Migration preparation failures should be able to report a fatal `error` reason separately from non-fatal `warnings`, and migration failure logging should preserve the original error details.

Existing legacy Quick Phrase data should be migrated into the new prompt list. Quick phrases from the old Dexie `quick_phrases` store should become prompts with their existing `id`, `title`, and `content` where valid, and should be assigned deterministic order keys preserving their displayed order. Invalid quick phrase records, such as records with missing or empty title/content, should be skipped with warnings rather than preventing the migration. Assistant-specific regular phrases and removed prompt-management concepts such as prompt versions, rollback, variables, and separate global/assistant prompt lists should not be migrated into the new prompt table.

The renderer should replace the Quick Phrase settings page and navigation entry with Prompt Management at `/settings/prompts`. The settings UI should load prompts from `GET /prompts`, allow creating a prompt with title and content, editing an existing prompt via `PATCH /prompts/:id`, deleting via `DELETE /prompts/:id` after confirmation, and reordering via the prompt ordering API. The create/edit form should use the prompt title and content placeholders and should submit only `title` and `content`. Prompt insertion from the quick panel should read from the unified prompt list rather than the old Quick Phrase service.

The legacy renderer-side `QuickPhraseService` and `/settings/quickphrase` route should no longer be used. Users should see Quick Phrase replaced by Prompt Management, with one unified list of prompt snippets.
